From: Mauro DiBenedetto <maurodibenedetto@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] TEST ONLY 0241: sled the pre-fix unbind_interrupt_level race window

Test instrumentation for the unbind_interrupt_level missed-suspend
reproducer, PRE-FIX form.  Holds open the window between the
pending-suspend flags test and the *INTERRUPT-LEVEL* restore, where a
suspend signal is deferred against the old level after the flags were
already read, so the unbind returns without delivering it.

MUTUALLY EXCLUSIVE with 0239 and 0242: this sled targets the original
instruction order and does not apply once 0239 has reordered it.  It
therefore lives in tools/fixtures/, NEVER in the patch series, and is
applied by hand to a scratch host tree for reproducer runs only.
NEVER DELIVER.
---

--- a/lisp-kernel/x86-spentry64.s
+++ b/lisp-kernel/x86-spentry64.s
@@ -3693,6 +3693,15 @@
 	__(movq rcontext(tcr.tlb_pointer),%arg_x)
 	__(movq INTERRUPT_LEVEL_BINDING_INDEX(%arg_x),%imm0)
         __(jc 5f)
+        /* TEST ONLY: hold this window open so a suspend signal can
+           land inside it.  ~100us at current clocks.  imm1 is dead in
+           the pre-fix hole and live in the post-fix one; save it in
+           both so the two sleds stay byte-identical. */
+        __(pushq %imm1)
+        __(movq $300000,%imm1)
+9:      __(subq $1,%imm1)
+        __(jne 9b)
+        __(popq %imm1)
 0:      __(testq %imm0,%imm0)
 	__(movq binding.val(%imm1),%temp0)
 	__(movq binding.link(%imm1),%imm1)
